Conflicts: satori-config
Replaces: satori-config
Description: Tekne desktop defaults and helper scripts
 System-wide defaults for the Tekne desktop: the X session
 (tekne-session), herbstluftwm autostart and keybindings, polybar and picom
 configuration, and startx on tty1. Defaults live in /usr/share/tekne and
 are used only when the user has no configuration of their own.
 .
 The Tokyo Night theme for herbstluftwm, polybar, rofi, dunst, alacritty
 (through tekne-terminal, the x-terminal-emulator alternative) and GTK.
 .
 Security and privacy defaults: an nftables firewall (tekne-firewall),
 Firefox ESR and Brave telemetry policies, and Wi-Fi scan MAC randomisation.
 .
 Helper scripts: tekne-run-once, tekne-keys, tekne-powermenu,
 tekne-screenshot, tekne-terminal, tekne-nmtui, and tekne-get-melia (downloads,
 verifies and installs the proprietary Melia email client on request).
 .
 On encrypted installs, tekne-autologin logs a user in on tty1 after the
 LUKS passphrase. startx on tty1 stops retrying for the rest of the boot
 when X fails at once, so a broken X can't loop through autologin.
 .
 Shell and session defaults for new users: bat as cat and fastfetch with
 Tekne's logo (through /etc/skel/.bash_aliases), ssh-agent keeping keys once
 unlocked, and XDG user directories. Nerd Fonts' symbols fonts for the bar's
 and terminal's icons.
 .
 elogind sleep hooks: TLP's suspend/resume handling, and a re-probe of ASUS
 N-KEY keyboards after resume.
